From d8e2d40e2a6f712a22b80bef91a900c9d7f5b433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:24:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/90] fix(ponder): make the dragged button follow the finger

Reported off the phone as "does not track the finger, cannot drag continuously",
and both halves were real:

- The drag wrote `left`/`top`. That invalidates layout on every move, and layout is
  main-thread work: the HUD on the same device shows 97 ms long tasks, so the
  button visibly trailed the finger. It is now `translate3d`, which only moves an
  already-composited layer, and `will-change: transform` keeps that layer alive.
  The position is still rounded and clamped in the same place.

- The button never set `touch-action`. Without it the browser is free to read a
  drag as a pan gesture, at which point it fires `pointercancel` and the drag ends
  where it was - literally "cannot keep dragging". `touch-none` claims the gesture,
  `select-none` stops a long press from turning into text selection, and the spec
  asserts the computed value because this failure cannot happen with a mouse.

The `transition-all` that used to cover opacity is narrowed to `transition-opacity`:
a transition on transform turns the drag into a rubber band. The pressed-scale
utility is dropped for the same reason - it shares the transform box now.

Position assertions in the component spec read the transform matrix instead of
`style.left/top`, and a seventh case pins `touch-action: none`.
